$( <MM> <PROOF_ASST> THEOREM=ef1lser  LOC_AFTER=?

* Term-by-term integration along a segment: if continuous ` F ( k ) ` on ` D ` are bounded on the segment ` [ A , B ] ` by ` G ( k ) ` with ` sum G ( k ) ` convergent, the line integrals of ` F ( k ) ` sum to the line integral of ` sum_ k F ( k ) ` .  Uniform convergence on the parameter interval (C5 ~ uhlim , the Weierstrass test) and ~ itgulm2 ; no dominated convergence.  The engine of Lean ` integral_right_edge ` .

